A check-argument log mode that costs a call per site instead of strings.

LV_CHECK_ARG_LOG_MODE_SITE routes every failed LV_CHECK_ARG / LV_CHECK_OBJ
through one cold lv_check_arg_failed_at(file, line), so each of the thousand-odd
check sites costs a call, not its condition text, function name and format
string. The check still runs and still takes its action; a failure logs
"Check failed" with the check's file and line. The ESP32 firmware selects it.

